# Story page: hive
# {name} becomes the snake's name. Paragraphs are separated by a blank line.
title = The Hive
---
Further on, the air began to hum, and then to buzz, and then to sound like an argument.

The Hive was full of honey and full of wasps, in roughly equal measure. The wasps did not care for {name}. They flew straight at its face, which I consider rude even by insect standards.

Among the wax lay a curious plate of grey metal, shaped like a scale. {name} wore it, and the next sting simply bounced off. Armor, it seems, is merely a scale that has made up its mind.
